cant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NEC CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, KENICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARA YOUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWATA RYUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUSAMITU HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MARUMOTO TSUNEHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI KENICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARA, YOUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWATA, RYUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUSAMITU, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MARUMOTO, TSUNEHISA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, KENICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A relatively small inexpensive phased array antenna provided even if the number of radiators is increased to enhance the gain. The phased array antenna has a multilayers structure including layers where a large number of radiators (15), phase-shifting units (16) each for shifting the phase of a high-frequency signal transmitted/received by the corresponding radiator, and a distributing/synthesizing unit (14) are provided respectively. Signal lines (X1 to Xm) and scanning lines (Y1 to Yn) are arranged on a phase control layer (35) to connect the phase-shifting units in a matrix. Selecting units (12X, 12Y) matrix-drive the signal lines and scanning lines to set a desired amount of phase shift for the phase-shifting unit located at the intersection. The circuits repetitively provided in the phase-shifting units are constituted of chips integrally mounted on another board.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette antenne en réseau à éléments en phase, peu coûteuse, est de taille relativement réduite même si le nombre d'éléments rayonnants a été multiplié pour accroître le gain. Elle est constituée d'une structure multicouche dont les couches sont pourvues d'un grand nombre d'éléments rayonnants (15) et de compensateurs de phase (17) déphasant, chacun, la phase d'un signal à haute fréquence émis/reçu par l'élément rayonnant correspondant. Elle comporte également un répartiteur/synthétiseur (14). Des lignes de signal (X1 à Xm) et des lignes de scannage (Y1 à Y n) sont montées sur une couche de commande de phase (35) aux fins de la connexion des compensateurs de phase dans une matrice. Des unités de sélection (12X, 12Y) commandent sur la matrice les lignes de signal et de scannage pour les amener à un seuil désiré de décalage de phase pour le compensateur de phase se trouvant à l'intersection. Les circuits montés de manière répétitive dans les compensateurs de phase sont constitués de microplaquettes faisant partie intégrante d'une autre carte.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>